WEBVTT

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.480
Coach!

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.990
Oh, it's you, Shigeno.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.880
The new school year has
filled out our team.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.700
Our first tournament starts today.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.500
It'll be the litmus test to see
if we can make it as a team.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.920
I think I've done what I can as captain
to prepare us, but I'm still full of doubts.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.660
We haven't got a replacement coach yet,

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:34.130
and I'm making it up as I go along,
so I'm worried how it'll turn out.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.510
It's good that you're worried.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.130
It's a leader's job to worry, 
and to remove those worries.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.600
But you can never let them
see it on your face.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.820
But...

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:51.570
Can someone like me, with very little
experience and skills, really rally a team?

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.320
You'll be fine.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.400
I know you can do it.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:35.170
<b>Captain Daigo</b>

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.170
Yes?

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:38.670
<i>Oh, wow! Is that the voice of the manager
of the national team, Satou Toshiya, I hear?</i>

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.500
<i>I'm pretty good at baseball.
Please put me on the team!</i>

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:47.060
You're not actually going to show up
and ask to try out, are you, Goro-kun?

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.850
Hey, that's a great idea.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.000
Hey, I'll be your batting
practice pitcher for free.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.140
<i>The frightening thing about
that is you actually would.</i>

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.650
Well, now that they've got a former
Major League home run king in their dugout,

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.320
the national team should be fine.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.860
<i>Go wild and show the world what you can do.</i>

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.120
Thank you.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.790
How's the Shikoku League?

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.460
It's good. I'm having lots of fun
with a lively bunch of people out here.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.500
<i>Glad to hear it.</i>

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:18.460
Oh, and there's another 
tournament starting today.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.590
<i>Led by their new captain, Shigeno Daigo,</i>

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.470
<i>Fuurin Middle's new-look team
is making its debut.</i>

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.810
Yeah... But I'm not worried.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.580
Daigo's got this.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.320
He's been working super hard
these past six months.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.110
<b>Fuurin Academy Middle School</b>

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.110
<b>Fuurin Academy Middle School</b>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.570
Our upperclassmen
got caught shoplifting?!

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:42.670
Yes.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:46.560
Nearly all of the second-years were
taken in and suspended from school.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.790
Which means they're off
the baseball team, too.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.250
You said "nearly all"...

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.960
I heard it was all the second-years
except for Tanba-san.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.140
No way...

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.630
Ah, there you are!

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.180
Tao! Yayoi! Have you heard?

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.590
We got the gist of it.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.790
This is terrible.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:08.170
We'd just started to rebuild
after the third-years retired.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.310
So this is all we have left...

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.770
We haven't picked our
new captain yet, either.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.530
How about you, Tanba-san?

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.580
Oh, I don't really...

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:23.240
I'm also on the Student Council,
and I don't think I'm good enough to be captain...

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:27.950
Coach!

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:32.650
I'm sure you've all heard
the talk going around by now.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:37.150
Only a negligent coach would let something
of this magnitude happen on his watch.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:40.140
I am truly sorry that I have done this to you.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:45.600
I've taken responsibility and 
resigned from my position as coach.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.050
You're going too?

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.660
As for what's left of the team,

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:56.520
I've talked to the school,
and you can still use the field for practice.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.610
But as far as competitive games go,

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:05.950
you won't play in any until next spring,
even if you scrape together enough players.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.080
For you, these circumstances are truly harsh.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.420
If at all possible,

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.370
I want you to inherit and
uphold the spirit and tradition

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:19.630
of the Fuurin Middle baseball team that
you've been absorbing these past six months.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.920
That is my final wish as your coach.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.630
Coach!

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.510
Well, there aren't any other clubs
I want to join, anyway.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:33.970
Besides, as first-years, we figured
we weren't going to get any game time.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:39.940
My final act as your coach
is to appoint a new captain.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.920
Shigeno, I'm entrusting you
with the captaincy.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:46.780
M-Me?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.620
<i>Shigeno-kun?</i>

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.910
B-But, uh... Why'd you pick me?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.320
Because I think you're
the most suited to the role.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.280
But you have a say in this too, of course.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:03.130
Think it over and come to a decision.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.920
Shigeno-kun!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:13.060
This is amazing!
You made captain as a first-year!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.840
It's not amazing at all.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.020
There's basically only first-years left.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.770
In terms of skill, Sawa-san and
Tao-san are both better than me.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.980
I don't have a clue why he picked me.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:25.420
Really?

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.580
I think you're a good fit.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.400
And we're all right behind you.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.870
I haven't decided if I'll do it yet.

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:35.450
Hey, Shigeno-kun, wait!

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.660
What?!

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.570
Almost all the senior players
got kicked out?!

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.630
And they're making you captain?

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.090
Shoplifting as a group?

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.430
Those twerps!

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:50.840
I shoulda disciplined them more
when they were first-years!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.040
But this is all so sudden.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.690
Will you be okay?

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.810
Captain as a first-year? 
That's a lot of responsibility.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.150
I'm going to quit the baseball team.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.140
Huh?

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:03.860
What?!

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.800
There's no way I can be captain.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.570
I'll quit the team and
play Senior League instead.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.080
You want to quit?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.280
But what'll happen to the team?!

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.260
We can't play in games, anyway,

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.910
so it doesn't matter if I'm there or not.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.650
The coach appointed you as the new captain.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:29.720
As an OG Fuurin player, I won't 
let you betray the team like that!

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.180
Oh, shut up!

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:35.320
You left Fuurin to go to a different
high school, so get off your high horse!

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:39.000
Yeah, because there was
no hardball girl's team!

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.390
Now, you two! No fighting.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:45.860
I joined the team because
I wanted to play baseball the right way.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.950
The team played at a high level,
with a solid coach and good senior players.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.340
It looked like I could really improve there!

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:57.560
And now, all of a sudden, we have
no coach and no senior players,

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.380
and we're not even allowed to compete.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.040
It's unbelievable.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:06.560
I understand where you're coming from,
but you should think it over.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.100
It's not just you who has to deal with this.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.720
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.720
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.720
Really?

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:15.180
The baseball team only
has five members right now?

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.800
Hey, that means I could
actually become a starter.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:19.970
Right?

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:21.640
This is a great chance!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.580
Maybe I <i>should</i> sign up, then.

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:27.980
So, Mutsuko, does it really 
help you lose weight?

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.120
Yeah, totally!

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.360
It's really great for losing weight!

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.320
Slenderly Kandori!

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.140
That could work!

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.400
<i>All right! Got one!</i>

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.610
Shigeno-kun!

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:42.790
It looks like the team's 
getting another member.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.870
A girl in our class called Kandori.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:48.220
Wait, aren't you coming to practice?

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:52.090
No, I've decided to quit the team 
and play in the Senior League.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.540
Could you let everyone know for me?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.520
Shigeno-kun...

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.300
I thought that was you, Pop.

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:08.230
I'm home.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.600
Hey, Daigo.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.570
Want to play catch after?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.080
You're bursting with energy, as usual.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.580
I heard the news.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:20.500
The newly-appointed captain
is quitting the team.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.000
You sure you wanna do that?

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:24.240
Why?

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.570
You gonna tell me
I'm being irresponsible, too?

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:28.020
Nope.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.570
Just thought it was a waste, is all.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.710
What do you mean?

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.600
With no coach and no senior players around,

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:38.280
you have the freedom to build 
a team the way <i>you</i> want it.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.680
You gonna throw a chance like that away?

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:44.880
I never particularly wanted 
to make my own team.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:49.350
And there's nothing wrong with joining
a strong team and shooting for a starting spot.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:54.450
But it's way more exciting
to take down stronger teams

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:56.540
with a team you built from the ground up.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.320
Isn't everyone waiting?

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.520
For you to make a move, I mean.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.610
That's so like Pop to say that.

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:15.210
After all, he transferred to a school
with no baseball team and built one there.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:20.300
But why do <i>I</i> have to build an 
entire team from the ground up?

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.090
Just so you know, I have absolutely 
no intention of copying Po—

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.930
That's good.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.600
You really shouldn't.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:31.160
That man has a sickness that makes him pick
the absolute hardest route in whatever he does.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:34.650
If you start copying him,
your life will become a living hell.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:36.360
O-Oh, really?

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.030
"Why do I have to do this?"

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:44.310
There was someone else who said
that when they made him captain.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.250
<i>Uncle Taiga...</i>

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.360
Hey, is that you, Daigo?

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.660
This <i>is</i> a surprise. What's up?

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.580
<i>My mom was telling me something...</i>

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.970
What'd my sister say?

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:03.410
You were captain of the Seishuu Academy
baseball team, right?

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:05.530
<i>Ah, yup, I was.</i>

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:08.430
She said you weren't too excited
about taking the role.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:12.650
Well, yeah.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:18.120
The Seishuu Academy baseball team was
the team of the indomitable ace, Shigeno Goro.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:22.790
When he graduated, we had no hope
of keeping up our winning ways.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:27.030
And I wasn't nearly good enough
to make the guys dream.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:31.980
But then your father said to me:

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:36.750
"Even losing in the first round is fine.
Build a team for you guys."

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.700
<i>And you said?</i>

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:42.140
Well, I got mad at him for being so idealistic.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:46.220
So I accepted the captaincy out of spite, 
dead set on losing in the first round.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:50.270
<i>Thinking back on it now, though,
I'm glad I did it.</i>

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:52.280
Why?

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:56.530
Because we overcame so much with that team.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:12:00.690
It made us a tight-knit group, I guess.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:05.730
<i>Or maybe I just really
loved baseball. Who knows.</i>

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:12.640
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:14.120
Just a little further.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:18.840
This was really hard for us at first, too.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:22.030
You two managed okay.

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.550
But it was so hard for me and Shigeno-kun!

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:29.020
I remember how we all used
to collapse after practice.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:32.670
Hey!

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:34.980
The first-years have to
put away the equipment.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.100
Coming.

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.740
Let's go, Shigeno-kun.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.400
No, I can't.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.180
Come on. Stand up!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.270
Seventeen!

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.850
This is a proper downpour!

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:58.860
I can't.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:01.030
Let's do thirteen more!

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.430
Eighteen!

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:17.200
I understand where you're coming from,
but you should think it over.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.400
It's not just you who has to deal with this.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.860
It made us a tight-knit group, I guess.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.070
Isn't everyone waiting?

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:29.490
For you to make a move, I mean.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:36.920
Pop!

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.510
Oh, hey, Daigo.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:41.250
What is it?

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:46.010
Pop... Please teach me baseball!

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:53.470
Please teach me baseball!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.830
Huh?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.580
Throwing. Catching. Batting. Running.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.690
Everything that's important to play it.

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:05.150
Coach me on the basics, the drills...
on everything you know!

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:06.920
Coach?

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.200
Come on, give me a break.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.950
I'm no good at teaching.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.660
I was given the captaincy.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.530
I have to push the team forward.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.840
But how can I do that
if I'm the worst player?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.980
We have talent to spare in our team.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:32.910
If I try really hard...
With everyone's combined efforts,

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:36.310
I believe we can drag Fuurin's
baseball team out of the abyss!

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.520
I see.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:44.730
I guess I can't run away 
after putting you up to this.

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:49.940
The only way I know how to learn
is through muscle memory.

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:51.210
Does that work for you?

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:51.970
Yes!

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:54.620
Here we go.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:00.000
Ow...

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.000
Huh? You say something?

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.880
Oh, uh... it's good we're practicing catching,

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:11.720
but isn't suddenly ramping up to 
catching a pro's pitches too big a step?

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.420
What are you talking about?

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:16.260
In the pro leagues, 
I pitched with my left hand.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:19.680
I only used my right in my Little League days
and when I was fielding.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.730
Yeah, but even so...

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:26.340
You learned all about catching 
from Toshiya, didn't you?

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:30.570
Now you just have to catch a load
of fastballs to get more experience.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.260
All right, I get it.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.750
Huh? Pop?

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.960
Nope. Don't wanna pitch to you anymore.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:48.980
You're catching them with
a face that says, "If I have to."

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:50.880
It totally kills my motivation.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.090
My... face?

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.770
It's the feeling. The feeling!

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:59.560
And you haven't even praised 
a single one of my pitches!

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:01.660
Are my pitches lifeless?

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:06.060
Are you thinking these are the pitches of a
decrepit old man with a busted shoulder? Well?!

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.300
I wasn't thinking tha—

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:10.780
Nice ball.

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:13.260
What the heck?

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:14.740
From the heart or not at all!

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:16.950
Nice ball!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:18.660
Right?

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:20.930
Nice ball!

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:21.710
Nope!

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:22.370
Huh?

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.340
That would've been a ball.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:27.090
I don't want you praising bad pitches.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.550
You're just being unreasonable now.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:33.260
'Course I am. Pitchers <i>are</i> unreasonable.

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:36.850
As my right hand, you need 
to know how to control me!

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:40.310
Get me hyped up!

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:43.640
Nice ball! Great!

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:45.620
Yup, that's good.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:52.900
Close. But you've got the speed.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.610
Nice one!

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:58.410
Almost...

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:02.200
Nobody could get near that last one.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.670
You got it! Just like that.

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.420
If the catcher hypes up the pitcher,

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:15.510
the pitcher will respond to it.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.960
Don't let it past you!

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.190
Put your life on the line for
your pitcher and stop them.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:30.280
Check out what's going on in the infield 
and the outfield, and talk the whole time!

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:34.320
You're the only one who sees the entire field.

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:38.670
If someone messes up, always
 get a clean hit when you're next up.

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:41.950
When the captain gets a hit, 
the entire team's mood changes.

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:47.690
Okay, okay.

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:48.830
You tired?

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:50.720
O-Of course I am...

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:54.190
Right! Starting tomorrow,
you'll do this every morning and evening.

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:54.800
What?!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.290
The captain has to train 
harder than anyone else.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:02.100
Nobody will listen to
a guy who's not training.

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:04.940
Chin up!

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.040
A captain must never look down.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.440
Y-Yes, sir!

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.860
You're starting to get it, Kandori.

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.910
R-Really?

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:21.320
Shigeno hasn't come for two weeks now.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:22.270
Yeah...

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.760
Didn't he say he was gonna
go play in the Senior League?

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:27.890
Doesn't that mean he quit?

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.580
Mutsuko, have you heard anything?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.440
It looks like he hasn't submitted 
an official resignation form yet.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.800
I asked him, but I didn't get an answer.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:40.760
If Shigeno quits,
we'll have to pick a new captain.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.630
Hard pass.

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:45.720
We can't compete, anyway, 
so do we even need one?

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.430
Of course we do.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.890
Then you can do it, for all I care.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.610
What's "for all I care" supposed to mean?

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.840
Shigeno-kun!

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.200
I'm sorry for being absent for so long.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:06.420
Carrying on in the team...
accepting the captaincy...

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:08.750
In my own way, I gave it a lot of thought.

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:11.990
I'm a first-year and have zero experience.

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:13.950
So my confidence isn't exactly high.

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:17.140
I'll be all at sea in every area.

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:20.120
But if I'm gonna do this,

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.840
I want to build a team that's stronger 
than any Fuurin team that's come before.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:26.140
With this roster, I know we can do it.

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.600
Will you all join me in trying?

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:31.930
Yes!

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:32.700
Yeah.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.550
I will.

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:34.540
Glad to be on board.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.570
Please.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:39.280
Thank you.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:40.520
One, two.

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:41.390
One, two.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.220
One, two.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.590
One, two.

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:46.160
W-Wait up...

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:47.470
Fifteen!

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:51.960
Safe!

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:02.380
All right, next!

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:03.600
6-4-3!

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:11.570
Okay! 5-4-3!

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:16.550
I knew it. I can't do this.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.960
This is too much for me.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.530
Sawa-san, can you take over hitting?

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:23.660
Okay.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.120
Kandori, come over here a sec.

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:29.830
Let's do a different set of drills
 until you get used to this.

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:31.340
You and me together.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:33.520
You don't have to do that!

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:36.270
I don't want to be a nuisance.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:40.870
I basically only signed up 'cause 
the team had so few players.

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.050
What are you talking about?

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:45.430
You're already an important part of this team.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:49.010
You chose our baseball team.
You chose baseball.

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:52.550
I want you to be glad you chose to sign up!

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:58.190
It doesn't matter how many
new members we get next month.

00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:01.650
Work hard and make sure you're a starter.

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:03.610
Y-Yeah!

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:06.580
Okay? I'll throw it slower for now.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.570
Try to catch it in front of your body.

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:09.680
All right.

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:10.460
Here we go.

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:12.040
That's it! Just like that!

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:13.810
I caught it!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:15.500
Okay! One more!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:17.500
Left field! Coming your way!

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:21.170
Don't worry.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.160
I know you can do it.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:28.580
You have a strong heart, 
and you're kind to others.

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:32.970
If you hold your head up high
and fight with optimism and energy,

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:35.560
I promise that everyone 
will follow your lead.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.090
Give it your all.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:38.520
I will.

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:40.790
Thank you very much!

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.230
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.230
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.230
Fujii

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.190
I'm leaving now.

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:47.750
Oh, Chisato, you've got a game today?

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:48.410
Yeah.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:54.580
If the Dolphins didn't have a practice game,
I'd come cheer for you!

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:55.370
Go get 'em.

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:56.580
Okay!

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.080
You too, Dad. Do your best.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.380
I will, don't you worry.

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:02.800
We got this!

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.680
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.680
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.680
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.680
<b>Sagara</b>

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:21.980
Just you watch.

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:23.980
Mifune Baseball Park

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:26.570
Let's go!

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:28.540
Yeah!

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:02.090
It's finally game day.

00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:03.370
How are you feeling, Tao?

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:05.380
Great, obviously!

00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:06.380
You are too, right?

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:07.470
Yuh-huh.

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:11.220
I also feel like their pitcher's
 totally looking down on us.

00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:14.620
That "as if we could lose to 
a team full of girls" vibe?

00:24:14.620 --> 00:24:16.100
It's on!

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:19.660
Then, let's show him how we play baseball.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:22.490
Next time: "Girl Power, Baseball-Style."

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Girl Power, Baseball-Style</b>

00:24:22.490 --> 00:24:24.640
Run to the stage of your dreams!
